568
00:25:40,820 --> 00:25:43,420
is the output a single vector?

569
00:25:43,420 --> 00:25:45,060
Does that [INAUDIBLE] have anything

570
00:25:45,060 --> 00:25:46,680
to do with the entire graph itself,

571
00:25:46,680 --> 00:25:49,820
or is there a reason why that output's a single vector?

572
00:25:49,820 --> 00:25:53,972
PHILLIP ISOLA: Yeah, for permutation invariance,

573
00:25:53,972 --> 00:25:55,680
the output could be more than one vector.

574
00:25:55,680 --> 00:25:56,972
