1485
01:06:19,310 --> 01:06:21,970
But let's get into the final section,

1486
01:06:21,970 --> 01:06:24,310
which is the theory of what kinds of functions

1487
01:06:24,310 --> 01:06:27,110
can GNNs approximate.

1488
01:06:27,110 --> 01:06:30,270
And the key question here is going to be,

1489
01:06:30,270 --> 01:06:33,097
which graphs can a GNN again distinguish?

1490
01:06:33,097 --> 01:06:34,680
And we'll see that they actually can't

1491
01:06:34,680 --> 01:06:37,000
distinguish all possible graphs from each other.

1492
01:06:37,000 --> 01:06:38,720
There will be these equivalent sets

1493
01:06:38,720 --> 01:06:42,120
where there'll be two different graphs where a GNN will

1494
01:06:42,120 --> 01:06:44,220
necessarily have to make the same prediction,

1495
01:06:44,220 --> 01:06:46,920
because according to GNN, those are the same graphs.

1496
01:06:46,920 --> 01:06:48,840
So what is the equivalent set.

1497
01:06:48,840 --> 01:06:52,500
So here are a bunch of graphs.

1498
01:06:52,500 --> 01:06:57,920
And you can imagine that from the perspective of certain types

1499
01:06:57,920 --> 01:07:02,920
of algorithms, certain sets of these graphs

1500
01:07:02,920 --> 01:07:04,618
will be seen as the same.

1501
01:07:04,618 --> 01:07:07,160
And we want to ask, which sets of graphs are going to be seen

1502
01:07:07,160 --> 01:07:10,320
as the, same as the graph that cannot make a separate

1503
01:07:10,320 --> 01:07:13,500
prediction on one graph versus the other graph,

1504
01:07:13,500 --> 01:07:16,240
if they're part of the same equivalence class?

1505
01:07:16,240 --> 01:07:20,760
So we're trying to understand what types of predictions

1506
01:07:20,760 --> 01:07:22,468
and functions graph nets can approximate.

1507
01:07:22,468 --> 01:07:25,052
And the way we'll do that is by showing that graph nets cannot

1508
01:07:25,052 --> 01:07:26,885
distinguish between certain types of inputs.

1509
01:07:26,885 --> 01:07:28,302
So they, necessarily, would not be

1510
01:07:28,302 --> 01:07:30,680
able to approximate a function that has to distinguish

1511
01:07:30,680 --> 01:07:33,340
between those inputs.

1512
01:07:33,340 --> 01:07:41,940
So yeah, the theorem is just a formal statement of that,

1513
01:07:41,940 --> 01:07:46,460
that if a graph net cannot distinguish between two items

1514
01:07:46,460 --> 01:07:48,300
in an equivalence class, then clearly,

1515
01:07:48,300 --> 01:07:52,020
it must incur an approximation error if the function I'm trying

1516
01:07:52,020 --> 01:07:55,540
to approximate does distinguish between those two graphs in that

1517
01:07:55,540 --> 01:07:57,120
equivalence class.

1518
01:07:57,120 --> 01:08:00,220
So what is the set of equivalence classes

1519
01:08:00,220 --> 01:08:02,380
for graph nets?

1520
01:08:02,380 --> 01:08:06,800
What graphs are considered equivalent to each other?

1521
01:08:06,800 --> 01:08:10,140
So the way to understand this is the tree structure.

1522
01:08:10,140 --> 01:08:14,980
So according to a graph net, that graph on the left--

1523
01:08:14,980 --> 01:08:17,939
according to-- any node that's trying to update its

1524
01:08:17,939 --> 01:08:21,020
representation based on messages coming in--

1525
01:08:21,020 --> 01:08:23,640
what it sees is these tree structures.

1526
01:08:23,640 --> 01:08:27,500
So the red node is going to see this neighborhood structure that

1527
01:08:27,500 --> 01:08:28,200
has that tree.

1528
01:08:28,200 --> 01:08:32,100
So it's connected on the first hop to the blue and green,

1529
01:08:32,100 --> 01:08:34,439
and on the second hop to all the other nodes.

1530
01:08:34,439 --> 01:08:36,979
And the green node is going to have that tree structure,

1531
01:08:36,979 --> 01:08:38,354
and the other green node is going

1532
01:08:38,354 --> 01:08:40,279
to have that tree structure.

1533
01:08:40,279 --> 01:08:43,600
So from the perspective of a graph net,

1534
01:08:43,600 --> 01:08:47,319
these trees are the entire characterization of that graph.

1535
01:08:47,319 --> 01:08:49,560
That's all they can see because that's how

1536
01:08:49,560 --> 01:08:52,120
the messages get propagated.

1537
01:08:52,120 --> 01:08:55,520
So if two graphs have the same tree structures

1538
01:08:55,520 --> 01:08:57,840
for all the nodes, then those two graphs

1539
01:08:57,840 --> 01:09:00,800
are equivalent according to the graph net.

1540
01:09:00,800 --> 01:09:03,359
So this may not be obvious, but it turns out

1541
01:09:03,359 --> 01:09:06,840
we can find two graphs that are different

1542
01:09:06,840 --> 01:09:08,560
and yet have the same tree structure.

1543
01:09:08,560 --> 01:09:11,200
And those two graphs will be two graphs that graph net cannot

1544
01:09:11,200 --> 01:09:13,377
distinguish, cannot make different predictions for.

1545
